    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="1139" n="1121" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg1121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/10–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-28T22:00:00-05:00">October 28,
                            1948—10 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4208. For Harriman from State and ECA.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d687-f1"/>
                        Bonesteel<anchor n="2" xml:id="d687-f2"/> refers to recent approaches by
                    Hall-Patch to Harriman and by Makins to Finletter on problem of correlation
                    Western Union rearmament with ERP (Dept of Army tel MA659 from Paris Oct.
                        18<anchor n="3" xml:id="d687-f3"/>). Only report on economic impact of
                    rearmament received here is account of discussion of Brit rearmament program
                    with Plowden<anchor n="4" xml:id="d687-f4"/> by Douglas and Finletter (London
                    Embtel 4315 Sept 29<anchor n="3" xml:id="d687-f5"/>). Current Brit thinking on
                    this subject and your views would be helpful in our consideration of
                    problem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d687-f1" n="1" xml:id="d687-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London for Douglas and Finletter as 4127.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d687-f2" n="2" xml:id="d687-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Charles H. Bonesteel, 3d, Executive Director of the European
                    Coordinating Committee of the Defense Assistance Program.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d687-f3" n="3" xml:id="d687-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d687-f4" n="4" xml:id="d687-f4-content">
                <p>Sir Edwin Noel Plowden, Chief Planning Officer and Chairman of the British
                    Economic Planning Board.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d687-f5" n="3" xml:id="d687-f5-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
